I still remember the first time I heard about ACID. 
I was in my last high school year when I first started to study databases. 
The second time was during the Database courses at university.

In both times, ACID was a key part of the lessons, but it was always treated from the Database user's view and never from the database's point of view itself.
In recent years, as a maintainer of Debezium, I'm more involved in database internals, 
I would like to write blank on white what I'm learning, hoping that it could be something useful not only for me. 

This is the reason behind this series of four articles focusing on how ACID is achieved in the databases. 

We will start with the "A" - Atomicity. 
